## Filter Tradeoff Observation

The moving average filter significantly reduced high-frequency noise in the gyro data, producing smoother signals.

However, increasing the buffer size introduced visible lag:
- raw gyro values reacted immediately to motion
- filtered gyro values responded more slowly

This occurs because the filter averages historical samples, causing previous data to influence the current output.

Conclusion:
Filtering improves stability at the cost of responsiveness.

