### Accelerometer-Based Pitch Estimation

Implemented pitch estimation using the relationship between filtered accelerometer axes.

Conceptually:

pitch = atan2(filtered_ax, filtered_az)

This converts the measured gravity vector into an estimated tilt angle.

---

## Observations

### Noise Reduction

The filtered pitch estimate showed:

* smooth continuous transitions
* reduced jitter
* stable behavior during slow tilt motion

The moving average filter successfully attenuated high-frequency accelerometer noise before angle estimation.

---

### Filter Tradeoff

Larger moving average buffers reduced noise further but introduced visible lag in angle response.

Observation:

* raw accelerometer values reacted immediately
* filtered values responded more slowly

This demonstrated the responsiveness vs. smoothness tradeoff present in all real-time filtering systems.

