## Critical System Insight

### Accelerometer Limitation

A major conceptual realization occurred during pitch testing:

The accelerometer cannot distinguish between:

* gravitational acceleration
* linear motion acceleration

This means:

* accelerating forward can appear as backward tilt
* braking can appear as forward pitch
* bumps and impacts can corrupt orientation estimates

While accelerometer-only pitch estimation works well during slow or mostly static motion, it becomes unreliable during dynamic movement.

